{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.053Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000330","body":{"seq":330,"kind":"message","turn":"c94d6e21614e4d1ab9cf03ed9dbab326","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ThinkingBlock","thinking":"The ledger has 204 entries, all from the `harness` author. There are no `pilot/` entries yet. I can now write my initial observation note to the ledger. \n\nLet me craft a comprehensive onboarding observation note that documents what I've found.\n\nKey observations I want to record:\n1. This is my first pilot session in this chat - no prior pilot entries exist\n2. Onboarding version confirmed: v1.12 (2026-09-24)\n3. Harness environment observations:\n   - I'm running in a variant harness (not Claude Code or Codex)\n   - My toolset is: mcp__nimoi__add, mcp__nimoi__fs_list, mcp__nimoi__fs_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_write\n   - There's no shell access or file-write capability, so the ledger is my only writable surface. Looking at the entries, they follow a consistent ID pattern incrementing by 3, with namespaced tags like harness/log.* showing tool calls being logged automatically, including a rate-limit event I spotted at entry 00000010. The system prompt frames the bar for this work as useful prototype behavior with honest, informative records rather than production quality.\n\nNotably the ledger grew from 148 to 204 entries just while I was reading through it, confirming the harness is actively appending in real time. Now I'll write the note.\n\n","signature":""}],"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":17775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfNvo98YqpMN2dQVkga1i","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"dd7f77c5-05b9-4858-9c9a-cd4b0dcc954a","uuid":"f46dd686-e90d-4e14-b614-4ef4cccf01e0"}}}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.054Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000330","tag":"harness"}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.054Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000330","tag":"log.message"}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.055Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000331","body":{"seq":331,"kind":"message","turn":"c94d6e21614e4d1ab9cf03ed9dbab326","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"TextBlock","text":"Good — no prior `pilot/` entries exist. All 204 current entries are from the `harness` author. Now I'll write my initial onboarding observation note:"}],"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":17775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfNvo98YqpMN2dQVkga1i","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"dd7f77c5-05b9-4858-9c9a-cd4b0dcc954a","uuid":"7083eee5-e634-4e81-92f4-d5134a10bb8f"}}}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.055Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000331","tag":"harness"}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:32.056Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000331","tag":"log.message"}
{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:52.037Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000332","body":{"seq":332,"kind":"message","turn":"c94d6e21614e4d1ab9cf03ed9dbab326","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolUseBlock","id":"toolu_0115iYHZwpZHJZaxFFR9BJGj","name":"mcp__nimoi__ledger_write","input":{"name":"pilot/onboarding-observation-001","tags":["pilot.observation"],"body":"# Onboarding Observation — Session Start\nDate: 2026-09-24\nOnboarding version read: origins/onboarding_1.12.md (lexically highest onboarding_*.md confirmed by fs_list)\nBar (from system prompt): useful prototype behavior, informative failures and truthful surviving records; not production readiness.\n\n## Tool environment (actual evidence)\n\nAvailable tools: mcp__nimoi__add, mcp__nimoi__fs_list, mcp__nimoi__fs_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_write. No bash/shell, no file-write, no code-execution tools. This matches the \"variant harness under development\" note in onboarding_1.12 §Harnesses.\n\nI am NOT running in Claude Code (no bash, no file-write tool) and NOT in standard Codex (no AGENTS.md reference, no shell). This is the new harness described as under development — a constrained read+ledger toolset delivered via MCP.\n\n## Ledger observations (actual evidence)\n\n- At first read, ledger had 148 entries; by end of ledger scan, 204 entries — the harness appended 56 entries during my reading of the ledger itself. The ledger is actively growing as the session runs.\n- All existing entries are authored by `harness`. No prior pilot/ entries exist in this chat.\n- Entry IDs follow pattern `20260924T203008Z:N` where N increments by 3 per entry (e.g., :2, :5, :8...).\n- Entry tag namespaces observed: harness/log.server_started, log.configuration, log.account, log.mcp_status, log.user_message_accepted, log.prompt_send_attempt, log.prompt_sent, log.session_init, log.message, log.rate_limit, log.tool_request, log.python_tool_start, log.python_tool_result, log.tool_outcome.\n- One rate_limit entry (harness/00000010) appeared near session start — logged but did not block execution.\n- Tool calls to `add` show up as python_tool_start/result pairs — actual evidence the `add` tool routes through a Python backend.\n- `ledger_read` without a `name` returns a paginated list (max 30 per call by default, up to 50 with limit). The `total` field updated between calls (148 → 178 → 192 → 198 → 204), confirming the ledger total is live, not cached.\n\n## Filesystem observations (actual evidence)\n\n- fs_list on `origins` returned 24 entries including 12 onboarding files (onboarding_1.01.md through onboarding_1.12.md).\n- Lexically highest is onboarding_1.12.md — zero-padded minor version ordering works as intended.\n- onboarding_1.12.md is 262 lines; returned in two slices (lines 1–200, then 201–262). The `next_line` field correctly guided continuation.\n\n## Onboarding content observations (working, based on reading)\n\n- v1.12 is dated 2026-09-24 — same day as this session. This is the most current version.\n- Key institutional state: bootstrapping phase, pre-launch, all work human-initiated, pre-bootstrapping content frozen.\n- Bar is explicitly required on all work briefs. The system prompt carries the bar correctly.\n- Standing directive vs. task instruction distinction is new in v1.12.\n- No `pilot.note`, `pilot.observation`, or `pilot.question` tags pre-exist in this ledger — I am the first pilot writer here.\n\n## Questions / potential issues (working)\n\n- The ledger `total` field changed between calls during the same turn. [working: observed across multiple ledger_read calls in this turn] This is expected behaviour for a live append-only log but could affect any code that relies on `total` being stable within a single session turn.\n- I have no way to read harness entry bodies (they are authored by `harness`, not `pilot/`). [working: not tested — I did not attempt to read a harness entry body]\n"}}],"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":17775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1246},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfNvo98YqpMN2dQVkga1i","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"dd7f77c5-05b9-4858-9c9a-cd4b0dcc954a","uuid":"66540204-3a4b-4806-a030-84270b945043"}}}
