{"ts":"2026-09-24T20:53:52.050Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"pilot/onboarding-observation-001","body":"# Onboarding Observation — Session Start\nDate: 2026-09-24\nOnboarding version read: origins/onboarding_1.12.md (lexically highest onboarding_*.md confirmed by fs_list)\nBar (from system prompt): useful prototype behavior, informative failures and truthful surviving records; not production readiness.\n\n## Tool environment (actual evidence)\n\nAvailable tools: mcp__nimoi__add, mcp__nimoi__fs_list, mcp__nimoi__fs_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_read, mcp__nimoi__ledger_write. No bash/shell, no file-write, no code-execution tools. This matches the \"variant harness under development\" note in onboarding_1.12 §Harnesses.\n\nI am NOT running in Claude Code (no bash, no file-write tool) and NOT in standard Codex (no AGENTS.md reference, no shell). This is the new harness described as under development — a constrained read+ledger toolset delivered via MCP.\n\n## Ledger observations (actual evidence)\n\n- At first read, ledger had 148 entries; by end of ledger scan, 204 entries — the harness appended 56 entries during my reading of the ledger itself. The ledger is actively growing as the session runs.\n- All existing entries are authored by `harness`. No prior pilot/ entries exist in this chat.\n- Entry IDs follow pattern `20260924T203008Z:N` where N increments by 3 per entry (e.g., :2, :5, :8...).\n- Entry tag namespaces observed: harness/log.server_started, log.configuration, log.account, log.mcp_status, log.user_message_accepted, log.prompt_send_attempt, log.prompt_sent, log.session_init, log.message, log.rate_limit, log.tool_request, log.python_tool_start, log.python_tool_result, log.tool_outcome.\n- One rate_limit entry (harness/00000010) appeared near session start — logged but did not block execution.\n- Tool calls to `add` show up as python_tool_start/result pairs — actual evidence the `add` tool routes through a Python backend.\n- `ledger_read` without a `name` returns a paginated list (max 30 per call by default, up to 50 with limit). The `total` field updated between calls (148 → 178 → 192 → 198 → 204), confirming the ledger total is live, not cached.\n\n## Filesystem observations (actual evidence)\n\n- fs_list on `origins` returned 24 entries including 12 onboarding files (onboarding_1.01.md through onboarding_1.12.md).\n- Lexically highest is onboarding_1.12.md — zero-padded minor version ordering works as intended.\n- onboarding_1.12.md is 262 lines; returned in two slices (lines 1–200, then 201–262). The `next_line` field correctly guided continuation.\n\n## Onboarding content observations (working, based on reading)\n\n- v1.12 is dated 2026-09-24 — same day as this session. This is the most current version.\n- Key institutional state: bootstrapping phase, pre-launch, all work human-initiated, pre-bootstrapping content frozen.\n- Bar is explicitly required on all work briefs. The system prompt carries the bar correctly.\n- Standing directive vs. task instruction distinction is new in v1.12.\n- No `pilot.note`, `pilot.observation`, or `pilot.question` tags pre-exist in this ledger — I am the first pilot writer here.\n\n## Questions / potential issues (working)\n\n- The ledger `total` field changed between calls during the same turn. [working: observed across multiple ledger_read calls in this turn] This is expected behaviour for a live append-only log but could affect any code that relies on `total` being stable within a single session turn.\n- I have no way to read harness entry bodies (they are authored by `harness`, not `pilot/`). [working: not tested — I did not attempt to read a harness entry body]\n"}
